!
! A note's order key, pinned first and then the most recent, in Trebago
! (margins_rules.h MR2): pinned * 253402300800 + stamp, so every pinned
! note's key is above every unpinned one's and, among the pinned or the
! unpinned, a later stamp (seconds since 1970) is a larger key; ranked by
! assay.score_rank (best first) the keys give the list's order. ok is 1
! for pinned 0..1 and stamp 0..253402300799 (the last second of year
! 9999), else 0, and the key is divided by it: anything else is a
! division by zero, refused, where key.kron answers: held.
trebago pinned_recent_key
  in  pinned(n), stamp(n)
  out key(n)
  var ok(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, pinned(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, 1 - pinned(i) + 1)) &
        * min(1, max(0, stamp(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, 253402300799 - stamp(i) + 1))
  key(i) = (pinned(i) * 253402300800 + stamp(i)) / ok(i)
end
